message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on a replica VW van used as a mobile food cart, with a 4kW electric motor. Candidate headings are 8703 (motor vehicles for transport of persons), 8704 (goods transport), and 8705 (special purpose motor vehicles). Mobile food carts are typically classified in 8705 as special purpose vehicles, though a vehicle that only moves 5-10 mph and is largely stationary could be classified elsewhere. I recall a CBP ruling that classified a similar item as a motor vehicle under 8705.90.

Within 8705.90, the subheadings are 8705.90.10 (cranes), 8705.90.30 (concrete mixers), 8705.90.50 (other), and 8705.90.60 and up for newer items. The "other" category is 8705.90.5000 with the statistical suffix, but I should check that. The HTSUS has 8705.10.00 (crane lorries), 8705.20.00 (mobile drilling derricks), 8705.30.00 (fire fighting vehicles), 8705.40.00 (concrete mixer lorries), and 8705.90 (other). Under 8705.90 there are 8705.90.10 (Mobile cranes) and 8705.90.30 (Tow trucks), and 8705.90.60 and 8705.90.80 (other). Specifically, 8705.90.30 covers "Vehicles specially designed for... " and 8705.90.60 covers "Other: Mobile... ". I'm not certain of these, so I'll go with 8705.90.8000 as the "other" category, which I believe is correct.

